## Bash Completion for Endpoint Paths

To make `bdapi` faster and safer for support engineers, you can enable **Bash tab-completion** for endpoint paths directly from the Postman collection.

### 1. Completion Script (`bdapi-completion.bash`)

Create a new file named `bdapi-completion.bash` in the repo:

```bash
# Bash completion for bdapi

_bdapi_complete() {
  local cur prev cmds endpoints

  cur="${COMP_WORDS[COMP_CWORD]}"
  prev="${COMP_WORDS[COMP_CWORD-1]}"

  cmds="list describe call"

  # Complete subcommands
  if [[ $COMP_CWORD -eq 1 ]]; then
    COMPREPLY=( $(compgen -W "$cmds" -- "$cur") )
    return 0
  fi

  # Complete endpoint paths for describe/call
  if [[ "$prev" == "describe" || "$prev" == "call" ]]; then
    if [[ -f "bd-postman-collection-public.json" ]]; then
      endpoints=$(jq -r '.item[] | .item[] | .name' bd-postman-collection-public.json)
      COMPREPLY=( $(compgen -W "$endpoints" -- "$cur") )
    fi
    return 0
  fi

  # Complete flags for call
  if [[ "${COMP_WORDS[1]}" == "call" ]]; then
    COMPREPLY=( $(compgen -W "--var --data --limit --offset" -- "$cur") )
    return 0
  fi
}

complete -F _bdapi_complete bdapi
```

---

### 2. Enable Completion (macOS / Bash)

From the repo root:

```bash
source bdapi-completion.bash
```

Or install permanently:

```bash
sudo cp bdapi-completion.bash /usr/local/etc/bash_completion.d/bdapi
```

Restart your shell or run:

```bash
source /usr/local/etc/bash_completion
```

